  "scope_id": "FOUR-PLACE-20261031-001",
  "title": "Value-free not-all-equal fails on regular systems only at three places",
  "subject": "Whether the knot's law, with signs, can fail on k-regular k-uniform systems for k >= 4",
  "conclusion": "For every k >= 4, signed not-all-equal never fails on k-regular k-uniform systems: a minimal failing system would be square with a sign-nonsingular incidence pattern, but its digraph has in- and out-degree at least 3 and is even by Thomassen's theorem. At three places it fails exactly on the knot's Pfaffian spaces, so Thomassen's degree threshold is the two/three boundary for this law.",
  "authority_class": "proof",
  "significance": [
    "exact_obstruction"
  ],
